Control statement
-----------------
The statement or instructions are used to inform the computer to perform the task when the program is being executed. There are 4 types of control statements : 

a. Sequential control statement
b. Conditional control statement
   (Decision control statement) 
c. Switch control statement
d. Looping control statement 

a. Sequential control statement
    input--------->process-------------->output
             (Formula implementation)
ex: p,r,t       si = (p*r*t)/100         o/p: si   

b. Conditional control statement
   (Decision control statement) 
        i. if statement
            syntax : 
                if(condition){
                    ....
                    ....
                }
        ii. if else statement 
            syntax : 
                if(condition){
                    ....
                    ....
                }else{
                    ....
                    ....
                }

        iii. nested if else statement 
        iv. else if ladder 

c. Switch control statement 
   -- It works on the concept of cases 
   -- It is mainly used for menu based programming 
   -- In javascript duplicate cases are allowed
   -- Here switch can consists of variable, constant and expression
   -- syntax :
        switch(variable | consstant | expression){
            case 1 : .....
                        break;
            case 2 : .....
                        break;
            default : ....
                        break;
        } 

d. looping control statement : 
Looping is the process of performing same task or some task in an iterative or repetative manner untill certain condition is satisfied.
There are two types of loops : 
        a. Entry control loop
        b. Exit control loop 

a. Entry control loop : Here condition is checked at the time of entry 
for loop and while loop comes under this category 

b. Exit control loop : Here condition is checked at the time of Exit
do while loop comes under this category 

also in javascript we some some more loops : 
        i. for in loop
        ii. for of loop 
        iii. for each loop 
